<title>USA: TWA September load factor drops.</title>
<headline>TWA September load factor drops.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trans World Airlines Inc said Monday its load factor dropped to 60.6 percent in September from 63.2 percent a year ago.</p>
<p>Short-term effects from the crash of Flight 800 pressured the load factor, the airline said. But in a news release, the company said it did not see that softness reflected in advance bookings for October and the winter months.</p>
</text>
